1
00:00:00,120 --> 00:00:01,960
You mean this guy Ken

2
00:00:02,080 --> 00:00:03,280
was at the bar on the 7th

3
00:00:03,400 --> 00:00:06,160
waiting to make a move on a girl.

4
00:00:06,280 --> 00:00:08,720
And that girl was the faceless corpse?

5
00:00:08,840 --> 00:00:11,040
I remember after my hike on the 8th,

6
00:00:11,200 --> 00:00:13,080
I bought something to drink at the store.

7
00:00:13,240 --> 00:00:15,440
At a distance, I saw a man chasing a girl

8
00:00:15,600 --> 00:00:17,520
and followed her up the hill.

9
00:00:46,520 --> 00:00:47,280
(Closed for 7 days for renovation)

10
00:00:47,400 --> 00:00:49,680
No...

11
00:00:56,360 --> 00:00:56,960
YY!

12
00:00:57,000 --> 00:00:58,080
Elsa!

13
00:01:02,920 --> 00:01:03,920
Are you OK?

14
00:01:15,880 --> 00:01:17,120
What are you doing here?

15
00:01:17,280 --> 00:01:19,360
Since you were so keen on finding Ken, so...

16
00:01:19,520 --> 00:01:21,040
I tried my way to find him.

17
00:01:23,160 --> 00:01:24,760
I went back to Tender Bar...

18
00:01:24,920 --> 00:01:26,160
Lee finally remember

19
00:01:26,320 --> 00:01:29,120
he always paid his tab with the
university credit card.

20
00:01:29,200 --> 00:01:33,840
Ken always used a credit card
from Hong Kong Island University

21
00:01:33,920 --> 00:01:34,960
to pay his tab.

22
00:01:35,120 --> 00:01:36,960
So I went looking for him at the university.

23
00:01:37,120 --> 00:01:40,080
I saw you when I arrived

24
00:01:40,160 --> 00:01:41,400
and I saw that guy.

25
00:01:41,520 --> 00:01:42,360
I guess he must be Ken.

26
00:01:42,400 --> 00:01:43,360
I was worried about you,

27
00:01:43,480 --> 00:01:44,800
so I sent you a message.

28
00:01:45,400 --> 00:01:46,720
Where are you now?

29
00:01:46,800 --> 00:01:47,840
But you didn't answer.

30
00:01:49,480 --> 00:01:52,040
You followed us because you were worried?

31
00:01:52,760 --> 00:01:55,600
I followed you here and saw you
go up the elevator.

32
00:01:55,800 --> 00:01:57,520
The other elevator was out of order

33
00:01:57,680 --> 00:01:58,840
so I took the stairs.

34
00:01:59,000 --> 00:02:00,760
I heard you screaming when I got up here.

35
00:02:00,880 --> 00:02:02,160
I broke the fire alarm

36
00:02:02,320 --> 00:02:03,840
to make him open the door.

37
00:02:04,360 --> 00:02:05,680
Luckily you found me.

38
00:02:05,840 --> 00:02:08,480
Lee already told me Ken was a creep.

39
00:02:08,600 --> 00:02:10,640
I can't believe I was stupid enough
to follow him here.

40
00:02:10,760 --> 00:02:13,440
Did you get hurt just now?

41
00:02:13,600 --> 00:02:15,920
I'm fine. As long as you're not hurt.

42
00:02:17,640 --> 00:02:18,560
You OK?

43
00:02:18,760 --> 00:02:19,360
I'm fine.

44
00:02:19,400 --> 00:02:20,640
We're stuck.

45
00:02:22,160 --> 00:02:24,800
Hello? We're stuck on the 5/F.

46
00:02:24,960 --> 00:02:26,640
Can you send someone?

47
00:02:26,840 --> 00:02:28,880
Right away.

48
00:02:30,120 --> 00:02:31,520
Don't be scared.

49
00:02:33,040 --> 00:02:34,960
I'm not because you're here.

50
00:02:36,840 --> 00:02:38,480
I'll watch over you.

51
00:02:51,640 --> 00:02:52,840
You OK?

52
00:02:54,280 --> 00:02:55,840
I'm fine.

53
00:02:59,760 --> 00:03:02,560
We fixed the voltage.

54
00:03:02,720 --> 00:03:04,000
The elevator should be working.

55
00:03:04,080 --> 00:03:05,200
Are you OK?

56
00:03:05,400 --> 00:03:07,040
We're fine. Thank you.

57
00:03:12,520 --> 00:03:14,320
Here's your phone.

58
00:03:14,440 --> 00:03:15,520
Thanks.

59
00:03:22,000 --> 00:03:23,360
There's still no signal.

60
00:03:23,720 --> 00:03:25,120
I have. I'll call the Police.

61
00:03:25,240 --> 00:03:27,200
What are you doing? No Police.

62
00:03:27,360 --> 00:03:28,840
I'll be in big trouble.

63
00:03:29,040 --> 00:03:31,280
He kidnapped you. No Police?

64
00:03:31,640 --> 00:03:33,440
I was anxious to find my sister

65
00:03:33,600 --> 00:03:35,680
and let Ken conned me out here.

66
00:03:35,840 --> 00:03:37,440
He didn't exactly kidnap me.

67
00:03:37,640 --> 00:03:38,880
This is not kidnapping?

68
00:03:39,040 --> 00:03:40,640
Did he ask you for money?

69
00:03:40,840 --> 00:03:43,520
That's kidnapping.

70
00:03:44,080 --> 00:03:45,840
No Police!

71
00:03:46,000 --> 00:03:47,280
Why are you so scared of the Police?

72
00:03:47,440 --> 00:03:49,040
Don't ask, OK?

73
00:03:49,800 --> 00:03:51,040
If you called the Police,

74
00:03:51,160 --> 00:03:52,840
you'll never see me again.

75
00:03:56,840 --> 00:03:58,440
I'll take you home.

76
00:04:09,200 --> 00:04:11,560
No need to take me home. I'll manage.

77
00:04:25,280 --> 00:04:26,480
Hello? I have the money.

78
00:04:26,560 --> 00:04:29,040
I'm on my way over. Don't hurt Elsa.

79
00:04:29,200 --> 00:04:30,400
Daddy, it's me.

80
00:04:30,520 --> 00:04:31,760
Elsa, don't worry.

81
00:04:31,920 --> 00:04:33,200
I'm on my way over to save you.

82
00:04:33,360 --> 00:04:35,440
Relax! I'm safe now.

83
00:04:35,600 --> 00:04:36,840
I got away already.

84
00:04:36,960 --> 00:04:38,560
I'm taking a taxi home right now.

85
00:04:39,080 --> 00:04:44,400
Good...that's really great...

86
00:04:46,080 --> 00:04:47,680
Why won't Elsa call the Police?

87
00:04:47,840 --> 00:04:49,680
Because of her sister?

88
00:04:49,840 --> 00:04:52,560
Not until Ken is arrested,

89
00:04:52,640 --> 00:04:54,960
he may come after Elsa again.

90
00:04:55,160 --> 00:04:56,840
I must find him.

91
00:04:58,080 --> 00:04:58,560
Elsa!

92
00:04:58,600 --> 00:05:00,000
Daddy!
Are you OK?

93
00:05:00,080 --> 00:05:02,480
You scared me to death!

94
00:05:02,840 --> 00:05:06,080
Your Mom went out.

95
00:05:06,400 --> 00:05:08,240
I dared not tell her about your kidnapping.

96
00:05:08,360 --> 00:05:09,640
I didn't want her to worry.

97
00:05:09,800 --> 00:05:10,800
Before she comes home,

98
00:05:10,880 --> 00:05:13,200
tell me exactly what happened.

99
00:05:13,360 --> 00:05:17,280
Last time I went to Tender Bar with Emma,

100
00:05:17,400 --> 00:05:21,120
I found out she had a boyfriend called Ken.

101
00:05:21,200 --> 00:05:24,000
It was Ken who kidnapped me.

102
00:05:24,200 --> 00:05:26,880
Emma had a boyfriend and didn't tell me?

103
00:05:26,960 --> 00:05:28,400
He kidnapped you?

104
00:05:28,520 --> 00:05:30,320
How did you get away?

105
00:05:30,400 --> 00:05:34,200
While he wasn't looking, I snuck out.

106
00:05:34,320 --> 00:05:38,160
Who is this Ken?

107
00:05:38,280 --> 00:05:40,320
Daddy, he's a creep.

108
00:05:40,400 --> 00:05:42,800
I think he might have kidnapped Emma.

109
00:05:44,200 --> 00:05:48,640
Elsa, I need to tell you something.

110
00:05:48,960 --> 00:05:54,400
I think...Emma is dead.

111
00:05:54,600 --> 00:05:57,440
Dead? How come?

112
00:05:57,720 --> 00:05:59,960
She just texted me she was safe.

113
00:06:00,080 --> 00:06:02,800
I think that text message

114
00:06:02,880 --> 00:06:05,840
was sent by someone posing as Emma.

115
00:06:07,800 --> 00:06:11,760
Ken killed Emma?

116
00:06:12,200 --> 00:06:16,880
No way, no way, Emma is smart.

117
00:06:16,960 --> 00:06:18,640
She must have gotten away.

118
00:06:18,720 --> 00:06:20,960
The Police came to see me at the hospital

119
00:06:21,080 --> 00:06:23,920
and asked me about chocolate cyst.

120
00:06:24,080 --> 00:06:27,840
On the faceless corpse,

121
00:06:27,960 --> 00:06:30,480
they found a 4cm chocolate cyst

122
00:06:30,640 --> 00:06:33,120
on the left side of the pelvic peritoneum.

123
00:06:33,280 --> 00:06:37,600
It was the same location as Emma.

124
00:06:37,800 --> 00:06:40,560
I'm sure that was Emma.

125
00:06:41,640 --> 00:06:47,600
Emma...

126
00:06:50,600 --> 00:06:54,800
Emma's death must be a major blow to Mom.

127
00:06:54,960 --> 00:06:59,360
When she comes home, let me tell her.

128
00:07:01,360 --> 00:07:05,920
We're heartbroken about Emma.

129
00:07:06,200 --> 00:07:10,000
But we must face reality.

130
00:07:10,720 --> 00:07:13,760
There's something very important...

131
00:07:13,920 --> 00:07:17,680
People must not know about Emma's death

132
00:07:17,840 --> 00:07:22,560
or the Police will show up at our doorstep
and find out about you.

133
00:07:23,200 --> 00:07:29,040
We must keep our normal life.

134
00:07:29,160 --> 00:07:31,920
If anyone should ask about Emma,

135
00:07:32,080 --> 00:07:34,480
just say she's studying abroad.

136
00:07:34,960 --> 00:07:39,680
I'll arrange for us to leave ASAP.

137
00:07:51,200 --> 00:07:53,120
I'll talk to you when I'm safe.

138
00:07:53,400 --> 00:07:56,960
Emma, please don't go.

139
00:07:57,200 --> 00:07:59,640
I don't want you to go.

140
00:08:00,200 --> 00:08:03,760
I'll contact you, silly.

141
00:08:16,400 --> 00:08:18,720
Elsa, since you're scared,
you can sleep with me.

142
00:08:18,840 --> 00:08:19,920
Great!

143
00:08:36,280 --> 00:08:37,200
That's him.

144
00:08:37,280 --> 00:08:39,040
He used a credit card from HKIU

145
00:08:39,200 --> 00:08:40,680
to pay his bar tab.

146
00:08:40,880 --> 00:08:43,440
So I used Ken and HKIU as key words

147
00:08:43,600 --> 00:08:46,960
and found his account.

148
00:08:47,160 --> 00:08:49,680
That's brilliant!

149
00:08:49,800 --> 00:08:53,120
He's with the Band Society at HKIU

150
00:08:53,320 --> 00:08:55,600
and has a studio in Wing King
Industrial Building.

151
00:08:55,800 --> 00:08:59,600
Wait, Lee gave you the address?

152
00:08:59,720 --> 00:09:01,520
I have my ways.

153
00:09:01,680 --> 00:09:03,920
Just like you have yours, right?

154
00:09:04,040 --> 00:09:05,680
You're doing my job?

155
00:09:05,800 --> 00:09:07,920
What matters is you can prove
he's the killer

156
00:09:08,040 --> 00:09:09,200
and get him busted.

157
00:09:09,280 --> 00:09:11,520
It won't be easy to prove someone
is the killer.

158
00:09:11,720 --> 00:09:14,720
But we'll bring him in for questioning.

159
00:09:14,920 --> 00:09:18,240
All our leads are dead ends.

160
00:09:18,400 --> 00:09:20,400
We can't even ID the body.

161
00:09:20,560 --> 00:09:22,320
We only found a watch in her pocket.

162
00:09:22,480 --> 00:09:23,680
What kind of watch?

163
00:09:23,880 --> 00:09:27,680
C628, with the initials EH engraved
on the watchband.

164
00:09:27,800 --> 00:09:31,120
It's probably the initials of her name.

165
00:09:47,720 --> 00:09:49,360
Emma, you said you were tired

166
00:09:49,480 --> 00:09:50,960
and didn't want to go to the spa with Mom.

167
00:09:51,120 --> 00:09:53,120
So unlike you to come to
the library with me.

168
00:09:53,320 --> 00:09:54,880
And you're reading that stack?

169
00:09:55,040 --> 00:09:56,800
Who says you must read them?

170
00:09:57,000 --> 00:10:00,400
I need them to rest my head so I can sleep.

171
00:10:00,480 --> 00:10:03,840
I can't believe you're doing this...

172
00:10:07,800 --> 00:10:11,520
Elsa...what's wrong?

173
00:10:12,480 --> 00:10:13,600
Nothing.

174
00:10:16,600 --> 00:10:18,720
You haven't been in touch.
Is Ken bothering you?

175
00:10:18,880 --> 00:10:21,360
No. Something happened at home. I'm busy.

176
00:10:21,680 --> 00:10:22,800
What happened?

177
00:10:22,920 --> 00:10:24,000
Nothing.

178
00:10:24,160 --> 00:10:25,040
Is it about your sister?

179
00:10:25,200 --> 00:10:26,240
No.

180
00:10:27,720 --> 00:10:29,200
I truly want to help you.

181
00:10:31,360 --> 00:10:32,960
Is this your sister's watch?

182
00:10:33,520 --> 00:10:35,200
That's a C628.

183
00:10:35,360 --> 00:10:36,560
Me and my sister each have one.

184
00:10:36,720 --> 00:10:41,040
We both had our initials EH
engraved on the watchband.

185
00:10:41,800 --> 00:10:43,280
Where did you get this picture?

186
00:10:54,680 --> 00:10:56,000
Where did you get this picture?

187
00:10:56,640 --> 00:10:59,360
Kwan Sir found it in the faceless
corpse's pocket.

188
00:10:59,440 --> 00:11:02,240
It had EH engraved on it, just like yours.

189
00:11:02,720 --> 00:11:06,000
Is my sister really dead?

190
00:11:06,280 --> 00:11:09,120
This is my feature assignment.

191
00:11:09,200 --> 00:11:11,280
That's why I've been following this case.

192
00:11:11,400 --> 00:11:12,880
As I dig deeper,

193
00:11:13,120 --> 00:11:15,760
I'm worried you might be involved.

194
00:11:17,000 --> 00:11:18,400
How did you know?

195
00:11:18,520 --> 00:11:20,480
You do your reading at the library.

196
00:11:20,640 --> 00:11:22,600
I suspect you don't have an ID card.

197
00:11:22,640 --> 00:11:23,600
Last time you went to Tender Bar,

198
00:11:23,760 --> 00:11:25,360
you left as soon as the Police showed up.

199
00:11:25,480 --> 00:11:27,760
When Ken kidnapped you,

200
00:11:27,920 --> 00:11:29,200
you refused to call the Police.

201
00:11:29,440 --> 00:11:30,920
There must be a problem.

202
00:11:31,400 --> 00:11:33,680
What happened at home?

203
00:11:34,360 --> 00:11:36,000
I can't tell you.

204
00:11:36,120 --> 00:11:37,920
I don't want my family in trouble.

205
00:11:38,480 --> 00:11:40,320
Because I know Kwan Sir?

206
00:11:40,920 --> 00:11:41,520
And because I'm a reporter?

207
00:11:41,640 --> 00:11:43,280
You have qualms about me?

208
00:11:44,920 --> 00:11:47,040
I won't force you,

209
00:11:47,280 --> 00:11:49,040
but I want you to know,

210
00:11:49,160 --> 00:11:52,800
I care about you not because
I have a story to write.

211
00:11:53,000 --> 00:11:54,960
I genuinely care about you

212
00:11:55,200 --> 00:11:56,720
and want to help you.

213
00:11:59,800 --> 00:12:01,760
You won't write this in your story?

214
00:12:02,360 --> 00:12:06,160
Everything you tell me won't go to print.

215
00:12:06,520 --> 00:12:08,720
You're my friend, I won't betray you.

216
00:12:09,360 --> 00:12:12,240
You saved me and have been a great help.

217
00:12:12,320 --> 00:12:14,640
You guessed most of it already.

218
00:12:14,800 --> 00:12:16,320
I might as well tell you.

219
00:12:16,440 --> 00:12:19,440
But you must promise you won't
call the Police

220
00:12:19,600 --> 00:12:21,360
or tell anyone about this.

221
00:12:23,200 --> 00:12:24,400
I promise.

222
00:12:26,280 --> 00:12:28,080
That's the gist of the story.

223
00:12:28,400 --> 00:12:29,680
After what happened to Emma,

224
00:12:29,880 --> 00:12:31,600
Daddy still won't let us call the Police.

225
00:12:31,680 --> 00:12:33,840
He was afraid they'd find out about us.

226
00:12:34,000 --> 00:12:36,160
But I'm not resolved.

227
00:12:36,240 --> 00:12:38,400
Ken was Emma's boyfriend.

228
00:12:38,480 --> 00:12:40,800
How could he kill her?

229
00:12:40,920 --> 00:12:42,800
Your sister was carrying so much cash.

230
00:12:42,920 --> 00:12:45,200
I'm not surprised he did it for the money.

231
00:12:45,280 --> 00:12:48,320
How can we prove Ken is the killer?

232
00:12:48,440 --> 00:12:51,760
You said he received your sister's messages.

233
00:12:51,920 --> 00:12:56,480
If Ken has her phone, that's enough proof.

234
00:12:56,640 --> 00:12:59,440
But how can we find Ken?

235
00:12:59,600 --> 00:13:02,240
What a shame we can't involve the Police!

236
00:13:02,400 --> 00:13:05,440
YY, why don't you tell Kwan Sir about me.

237
00:13:05,560 --> 00:13:07,840
Then he'll know Ken is related to Emma.

238
00:13:07,920 --> 00:13:10,800
But we can't tell him you have no ID

239
00:13:10,920 --> 00:13:12,880
or the victim was your sister.

240
00:13:13,000 --> 00:13:14,400
That would be tough.

241
00:13:14,920 --> 00:13:16,720
I already gave Kwan Sir a hint

242
00:13:16,840 --> 00:13:18,480
Ken is dangerous.

243
00:13:18,680 --> 00:13:20,480
If he's keeping tabs on him,

244
00:13:20,600 --> 00:13:22,240
I think you should be safe.

245
00:13:22,440 --> 00:13:24,560
I don't want Emma to die
under dubious circumstances.

246
00:13:24,760 --> 00:13:27,040
Help me figure something out, YY.

247
00:13:27,200 --> 00:13:28,480
Don't worry!

248
00:13:28,680 --> 00:13:31,680
I'll do my best to find Ken.

249
00:13:31,800 --> 00:13:34,480
I'll tell Kwan Sir once I found him, OK?

250
00:13:40,280 --> 00:13:44,640
Oh dear. It's Daddy. I must go.

251
00:13:44,760 --> 00:13:45,760
I'll take you home.

252
00:13:45,920 --> 00:13:48,800
No. I don't want Daddy to know about you.

253
00:13:49,040 --> 00:13:50,640
I'll go home by myself.

254
00:13:56,240 --> 00:13:58,320
We're mourning your sister.

255
00:13:58,440 --> 00:14:00,920
Come and say goodbye to her.

256
00:14:04,760 --> 00:14:09,920
Emma...I missed you so much.

257
00:14:10,320 --> 00:14:14,640
You said you'll always be my sister.

258
00:14:15,760 --> 00:14:19,120
You'll always be in my heart.

259
00:14:20,320 --> 00:14:27,840
Emma died a horrible death.

260
00:14:28,000 --> 00:14:31,280
I want to release her from suffering.

261
00:14:31,840 --> 00:14:38,160
I already told you we must act normal.

262
00:14:38,320 --> 00:14:40,480
We can't do anything out of the ordinary.

263
00:14:42,680 --> 00:14:45,520
Besides, we're leaving next week.

264
00:14:45,720 --> 00:14:49,040
So quick? Can you manage?

265
00:14:49,240 --> 00:14:52,480
I took one week off.

266
00:14:52,840 --> 00:14:54,640
When we're safe and settled down,

267
00:14:54,800 --> 00:14:56,640
I'll call the hospital and quit.

268
00:14:56,760 --> 00:15:00,320
The rest are pretty much taken care of.

269
00:15:00,480 --> 00:15:02,640
Is there no other way?

270
00:15:02,800 --> 00:15:04,960
We can't just pack up and leave!

271
00:15:05,080 --> 00:15:06,640
We must leave while we can.

272
00:15:06,800 --> 00:15:08,320
What are we waiting for?

273
00:15:09,000 --> 00:15:11,440
We haven't caught Emma's killer.

274
00:15:11,600 --> 00:15:13,120
I'm not leaving.

275
00:15:13,280 --> 00:15:15,760
I want to know how she died.

276
00:15:15,840 --> 00:15:17,280
If the Police caught the killer,

277
00:15:17,400 --> 00:15:19,360
we'll find out wherever we are.

278
00:15:19,440 --> 00:15:21,360
What's the use of waiting around?

279
00:15:21,640 --> 00:15:23,280
If we want the family intact,

280
00:15:23,440 --> 00:15:25,040
we must leave together.

281
00:15:25,120 --> 00:15:26,880
Emma is gone.

282
00:15:27,000 --> 00:15:29,440
The family is not intact.

283
00:15:32,800 --> 00:15:38,560
Elsa...if we don't leave together,

284
00:15:38,680 --> 00:15:42,400
this family will fall apart.

285
00:15:42,920 --> 00:15:45,840
Elsa, I can't afford to lose you, too.

286
00:15:46,040 --> 00:15:48,720
Please leave with us, OK?

287
00:15:50,320 --> 00:15:51,760
OK?

288
00:16:02,640 --> 00:16:05,280
We don't care who the killer was?

289
00:16:05,400 --> 00:16:08,080
We do nothing about Emma's death?

290
00:16:11,880 --> 00:16:12,560
Hello?

291
00:16:12,680 --> 00:16:14,240
Elsa, I found a way

292
00:16:14,400 --> 00:16:16,560
to know your sister's whereabouts.

293
00:16:16,760 --> 00:16:18,160
If we know where she has been,

294
00:16:18,320 --> 00:16:19,760
there's a chance we'll find Ken.

295
00:16:19,960 --> 00:16:20,960
How?

296
00:16:22,120 --> 00:16:22,920
(Transactions for past 30 days)

297
00:16:22,960 --> 00:16:23,920
I wouldn't know if you didn't tell me,

298
00:16:24,040 --> 00:16:27,280
Emma linked her Hong Kong Pass
account to her email.

299
00:16:27,400 --> 00:16:28,560
I sent an email

300
00:16:28,680 --> 00:16:30,400
and accessed her transaction records.

301
00:16:30,560 --> 00:16:33,360
Luckily, she used the same password

302
00:16:33,440 --> 00:16:34,480
for her email and Instabook,

303
00:16:34,640 --> 00:16:36,480
or else you couldn't have logged in.

304
00:16:36,680 --> 00:16:38,480
Check the invoices now.

305
00:16:40,440 --> 00:16:43,520
It says here, the first day Emma left,

306
00:16:43,680 --> 00:16:47,080
she went to restaurants,
convenience stores and bars.

307
00:16:47,240 --> 00:16:49,840
Up until Day 3,

308
00:16:50,000 --> 00:16:51,840
I can see all the transactions.

309
00:16:51,920 --> 00:16:53,120
You're brilliant, YY!

310
00:16:53,240 --> 00:16:55,280
We must check out all these places.

311
00:16:55,360 --> 00:17:00,320
But Emma stopped using this card
after the third night.

312
00:17:00,440 --> 00:17:03,640
Should we focus on Day 3?

313
00:17:04,040 --> 00:17:06,720
I'm not busy tomorrow.

314
00:17:06,920 --> 00:17:08,200
I'll go with you tomorrow.

315
00:17:08,320 --> 00:17:10,040
I'm not sure if I could come out.

316
00:17:10,120 --> 00:17:13,760
It's OK. Mom is not feeling well lately.

317
00:17:13,880 --> 00:17:16,880
I can wait till she takes her
sleeping pills and goes to bed

318
00:17:16,960 --> 00:17:18,600
before I sneak outside.

319
00:17:18,760 --> 00:17:20,800
It's OK. I'll start checking.

320
00:17:20,880 --> 00:17:23,200
I can't talk now. I need to work.

321
00:17:23,320 --> 00:17:24,640
Bye!

322
00:17:25,120 --> 00:17:25,920
Bye!

323
00:17:29,280 --> 00:17:31,120
I better not tell him I'm leaving.

324
00:17:31,240 --> 00:17:32,480
Let's focus on finding Ken.

325
00:17:52,480 --> 00:17:54,240
(The next day)

326
00:17:55,440 --> 00:17:56,360
Hello, YY!

327
00:17:56,560 --> 00:18:01,920
That night, your sister ate at this
pizza place.

328
00:18:02,000 --> 00:18:06,880
The waitress said she was alone.

329
00:18:07,400 --> 00:18:08,840
You went out so early?

330
00:18:08,960 --> 00:18:12,360
I want to visit all the places your sister
went to within today.

331
00:18:12,480 --> 00:18:14,360
The sooner I find Ken,
the safer you will be.

332
00:18:14,520 --> 00:18:16,840
You hit every place on the list?'

333
00:18:16,960 --> 00:18:18,400
You're so efficient.

334
00:18:18,600 --> 00:18:21,560
I'm a special agent held up
by his reporter's duties.

335
00:18:21,720 --> 00:18:26,640
CIX, MIA and MIB are trying to recruit me.

336
00:18:26,840 --> 00:18:29,280
What have you found out, Agent YY?

337
00:18:29,440 --> 00:18:30,720
Nothing yet.

338
00:18:30,920 --> 00:18:33,360
Don't worry, just a few more on the list.

339
00:18:33,520 --> 00:18:36,160
I'll find Ken for sure within the day.

340
00:18:47,000 --> 00:18:48,160
Why is it shaking?

341
00:18:48,320 --> 00:18:50,800
Elsa, sorry! You're in my behind.

342
00:18:51,040 --> 00:18:52,040
What?

343
00:18:52,200 --> 00:18:54,400
I'm helping a pretty girl with
some heavy lifting. No hands.

344
00:18:54,480 --> 00:18:57,360
I have a few more boxes. Talk to you later.

345
00:18:57,520 --> 00:18:59,600
Thanks, handsome. This is for you.

346
00:18:59,680 --> 00:19:00,800
I should thank you.

347
00:19:01,800 --> 00:19:02,640
Well?

348
00:19:02,760 --> 00:19:04,880
Elsa, one good turn deserves another.

349
00:19:05,080 --> 00:19:08,040
The pretty girl remembers your sister
came by on the 6th.

350
00:19:08,200 --> 00:19:12,000
She mentioned she was going to
Par Par Party Room.

351
00:19:19,400 --> 00:19:22,320
Hello, are you here for Zita's
birthday party?

352
00:19:22,400 --> 00:19:24,720
No, we're looking for someone.

353
00:19:24,840 --> 00:19:26,800
Between the 6th and the 12th,

354
00:19:26,880 --> 00:19:28,400
have you seen this girl?

355
00:19:28,720 --> 00:19:29,920
No.

356
00:19:30,080 --> 00:19:32,400
I'm sure she was here.

357
00:19:32,560 --> 00:19:35,120
Can you please look again? It's important.

358
00:19:35,280 --> 00:19:37,760
The venue is booked for a birthday party.

359
00:19:37,920 --> 00:19:40,320
I'm sorry I can't help you.

360
00:19:40,600 --> 00:19:43,520
Hello, are you the performing guests?

361
00:19:43,600 --> 00:19:44,240
Yes!

362
00:19:44,360 --> 00:19:45,200
You can set up over here.

363
00:19:45,320 --> 00:19:46,160
Thanks.

364
00:19:48,000 --> 00:19:51,040
Sorry, can we see your CCTV?

365
00:19:51,200 --> 00:19:52,840
Who are you?

366
00:19:52,960 --> 00:19:55,360
The CCTV involves privacy issues.

367
00:19:55,480 --> 00:19:57,040
We can't show it to you.

368
00:19:57,240 --> 00:19:58,120
Thanks.

369
00:19:58,400 --> 00:20:00,360
I wonder if Zita invited Ken.

370
00:20:00,480 --> 00:20:03,320
He disappeared after he borrowed
a few thousand dollars from me.

371
00:20:03,400 --> 00:20:07,040
He lost all the money he borrowed from
the finance company in the stock market.

372
00:20:07,120 --> 00:20:08,160
Why did you lend him money?

373
00:20:08,360 --> 00:20:10,520
We better start looking for
another bass guitarist.

374
00:20:10,600 --> 00:20:12,800
Excuse me...the Ken you were
talking about,

375
00:20:12,880 --> 00:20:14,840
is he from the HKIU Band Society?

376
00:20:15,000 --> 00:20:18,400
Yes, he's in our band from school.

377
00:20:18,600 --> 00:20:20,040
We're looking for Ken.

378
00:20:20,200 --> 00:20:21,800
Do you know where I can find him?

379
00:20:21,920 --> 00:20:26,000
I saw him with a girl last week
in Tsimshatsui.

380
00:20:26,080 --> 00:20:28,040
With her?

381
00:20:28,120 --> 00:20:28,880
I think so.

382
00:20:29,040 --> 00:20:30,720
Do you remember where in Tsimshatsui?

383
00:20:30,880 --> 00:20:34,320
Somewhere near a guesthouse.

384
00:20:34,400 --> 00:20:36,280
But I forgot the name.

385
00:20:36,480 --> 00:20:37,600
Anything nearby you remember?

386
00:20:37,640 --> 00:20:39,840
Nearby?
Thanks.

387
00:20:39,920 --> 00:20:41,840
What? I'm not finished...
Police!

388
00:20:42,880 --> 00:20:45,120
Who's in charge?

389
00:20:45,360 --> 00:20:46,960
Sir, what is it?

390
00:20:47,040 --> 00:20:48,160
Someone called the Police

391
00:20:48,280 --> 00:20:49,680
and reported a missing diamond ring.

392
00:20:49,800 --> 00:20:50,760
Who made the call?

393
00:20:50,840 --> 00:20:52,080
I did.

394
00:20:52,320 --> 00:20:55,520
Before I went to the toilet,
I left the ring on the table.

395
00:20:55,600 --> 00:20:58,400
When I came out, it was gone.

396
00:20:58,560 --> 00:21:00,320
I need you all to step over here.

397
00:21:00,440 --> 00:21:01,560
Get your ID cards ready.

398
00:21:01,600 --> 00:21:03,840
Let us take your names and statements.

399
00:21:09,960 --> 00:21:11,760
Hey, you two! Where are you going?

400
00:21:11,840 --> 00:21:13,120
Stop! Come back...

401
00:21:14,080 --> 00:21:15,440
You OK?
I'm fine.

402
00:21:34,840 --> 00:21:35,840
Where did they go?

403
00:21:36,400 --> 00:21:37,760
Let's go that way.

404
00:21:47,200 --> 00:21:48,480
I think they're gone.

405
00:22:15,080 --> 00:22:19,360
It's late. I should head home.

406
00:22:20,040 --> 00:22:24,520
I'll try to sneak out again tomorrow
and we'll go look.

407
00:22:25,320 --> 00:22:27,520
OK!

408
00:22:28,600 --> 00:22:30,800
I'll check out the guest houses in the area.

409
00:22:36,080 --> 00:22:38,120
Bye!

410
00:22:38,840 --> 00:22:40,040
Bye!

411
00:22:58,400 --> 00:23:00,000
Luckily, Daddy is not home yet.

412
00:23:00,120 --> 00:23:02,880
I'll go change and check on Mom.

413
00:23:09,040 --> 00:23:12,120
We haven't hugged and chatted for so long.

414
00:23:15,000 --> 00:23:18,720
Did you go out just now?

415
00:23:19,000 --> 00:23:22,280
Since you were asleep,
I went to the library.

416
00:23:22,360 --> 00:23:25,120
At this hour? What for?

417
00:23:26,160 --> 00:23:28,560
Did something happen?

418
00:23:28,640 --> 00:23:30,960
No, nothing happened.

419
00:23:31,680 --> 00:23:35,200
You know you can always talk to me.

420
00:23:36,840 --> 00:23:40,720
Let me ask you a hypothetical question.

421
00:23:40,880 --> 00:23:43,200
Given my background,

422
00:23:43,320 --> 00:23:47,360
if and when I meet a guy I like,

423
00:23:47,520 --> 00:23:50,720
what are my chances of starting
a relationship with him?

424
00:23:52,640 --> 00:23:56,880
If you knew there will be problems

425
00:23:57,040 --> 00:23:59,560
and still went ahead to
start a relationship,

426
00:23:59,720 --> 00:24:05,440
it's hard to say if it's a good thing.

427
00:24:05,520 --> 00:24:06,880
I don't get it.

428
00:24:07,160 --> 00:24:09,080
It's enough that we're in love.

429
00:24:09,200 --> 00:24:11,840
I was lucky to have met Daddy.

430
00:24:12,000 --> 00:24:15,200
He's a very good man

431
00:24:15,400 --> 00:24:17,640
and he loves me very much.

432
00:24:18,000 --> 00:24:25,200
Unfortunately, we met at the
wrong time and wrong place.

433
00:24:25,280 --> 00:24:26,640
What do you mean?

434
00:24:26,760 --> 00:24:30,360
You've always been happy with Daddy.

435
00:24:30,600 --> 00:24:32,160
Remember you asked me before

436
00:24:32,280 --> 00:24:34,400
why I didn't return to my homeland?

437
00:24:35,200 --> 00:24:39,200
I wanted to, but I can't.

438
00:24:39,960 --> 00:24:41,840
I was married to a drunk.

439
00:24:41,920 --> 00:24:45,080
He used to beat me up when he lost
money in gambling.

440
00:24:45,400 --> 00:24:49,120
You divorced him to marry Daddy?

441
00:24:49,280 --> 00:24:51,640
Daddy and I were never registered
for marriage.

442
00:24:51,920 --> 00:24:54,240
In order to pay for that creep's debts,

443
00:24:54,360 --> 00:24:56,520
he made me a whore.

444
00:24:56,960 --> 00:25:00,960
I thought I would spend the rest
of my life like that.

445
00:25:01,160 --> 00:25:05,320
But Heaven opened another door for me.

446
00:25:05,480 --> 00:25:09,440
A good friend found me a job here.

447
00:25:09,600 --> 00:25:15,440
I secretly left that creep and came
to Hong Kong

448
00:25:15,560 --> 00:25:18,320
where I met Daddy

449
00:25:18,560 --> 00:25:21,120
and we decided to be together.

450
00:25:21,840 --> 00:25:24,040
Can't you just go back and
divorce that creep?

451
00:25:24,080 --> 00:25:26,360
Because of my homeland's religious belief,

452
00:25:26,440 --> 00:25:27,920
divorce is not allowed.

453
00:25:28,120 --> 00:25:30,160
Daddy didn't want me to go back.

454
00:25:30,360 --> 00:25:34,280
I stayed in Hong Kong and eventually
overstayed my visa.

455
00:25:34,360 --> 00:25:38,240
That's why Emma and I can't get an ID card.

456
00:25:38,400 --> 00:25:40,960
I was selfish.

457
00:25:41,320 --> 00:25:42,960
Without an ID card,

458
00:25:43,120 --> 00:25:45,360
there's so much you can't do.

459
00:25:45,480 --> 00:25:47,120
You should come to my homeland with me

460
00:25:47,240 --> 00:25:50,080
so you can get an ID card.

461
00:25:50,400 --> 00:25:52,440
Though I don't have an ID card,

462
00:25:52,480 --> 00:25:58,800
if I met someone who loves me
as much as Daddy loves you,

463
00:25:58,920 --> 00:25:59,840
it'll be OK.

464
00:26:00,000 --> 00:26:03,040
It's not that simple, silly.

465
00:26:03,160 --> 00:26:06,880
I don't want you to go through life
like I did.

466
00:26:07,080 --> 00:26:08,760
You should come with me.

467
00:26:12,560 --> 00:26:15,200
I'd like you to meet a friend
from my homeland

468
00:26:15,320 --> 00:26:17,920
who will help us go home.

469
00:26:18,080 --> 00:26:21,600
Mom, I'm a bit tired.

470
00:26:21,720 --> 00:26:23,440
I'll wait for you at home.

471
00:26:23,560 --> 00:26:26,880
OK, go on home.

472
00:26:27,920 --> 00:26:30,040
See you later.
See you.

473
00:26:35,200 --> 00:26:37,360
I forgot to buy cheese.

474
00:26:43,520 --> 00:26:46,000
I thought she was going home.

475
00:26:46,080 --> 00:26:48,160
Why is she going to Tsimshatsui?

476
00:26:52,640 --> 00:26:54,000
Before I leave,

477
00:26:54,080 --> 00:26:56,640
I must try to find Ken with YY.

478
00:26:56,800 --> 00:26:58,640
I want to see more of him.

479
00:27:05,360 --> 00:27:06,960
(Bo On Hotel)

480
00:27:10,720 --> 00:27:13,600
(Bo On Hotel)

481
00:27:20,720 --> 00:27:22,320
Hello, folks.

482
00:27:22,440 --> 00:27:23,920
By the hour or spend the night?

483
00:27:24,120 --> 00:27:26,320
No, we're looking for someone.

484
00:27:26,560 --> 00:27:27,920
Have you seen him?

485
00:27:28,040 --> 00:27:30,600
And what if I did?

486
00:27:30,760 --> 00:27:34,480
Can we watch your CCTV?

487
00:27:34,640 --> 00:27:37,040
No problem. This guy's name is Ken.

488
00:27:37,120 --> 00:27:40,480
He came with a chick.

489
00:27:40,720 --> 00:27:42,120
Emma!

490
00:27:42,280 --> 00:27:45,280
Here's the CCTV. Go to Room 1.

491
00:27:51,520 --> 00:27:52,720
Here...

492
00:27:54,800 --> 00:27:56,960
(Day 1 after Emma left)

493
00:27:57,040 --> 00:27:59,200
That's Emma! She was here.

494
00:28:00,360 --> 00:28:03,040
Why didn't Ken stay with her?

495
00:28:06,440 --> 00:28:08,880
(Day 2 after Emma left)

496
00:28:11,280 --> 00:28:12,960
Where did she go by herself?

497
00:28:15,880 --> 00:28:17,760
(Second night after Emma left)

498
00:28:17,880 --> 00:28:19,600
She was alone the whole time.

499
00:28:19,960 --> 00:28:22,120
Why didn't Ken come back with her?

500
00:28:22,200 --> 00:28:24,120
(Day 3 after Emma left)

501
00:28:25,840 --> 00:28:27,760
Ken was not with her at all. That's odd.

502
00:28:30,360 --> 00:28:32,840
(Day 3 after Emma left at 5:00 pm)

503
00:28:33,480 --> 00:28:34,960
That's Ken!

504
00:28:38,400 --> 00:28:40,400
Why did he steal the key?

505
00:28:44,440 --> 00:28:47,440
He went inside Emma's room!

506
00:28:47,520 --> 00:28:48,880
YY, fast forward.

507
00:28:50,880 --> 00:28:52,400
(2 minutes later)

508
00:28:52,520 --> 00:28:53,680
There's Emma!

509
00:28:53,800 --> 00:28:56,000
Fast forward and see what happened.

510
00:29:00,960 --> 00:29:03,200
That's Emma! Was she bleeding?

511
00:29:05,200 --> 00:29:06,320
Yes!

512
00:29:06,400 --> 00:29:07,640
What happened?

513
00:29:10,360 --> 00:29:12,000
Why did she leave in a hurry?

514
00:29:18,400 --> 00:29:19,520
It's Ken!

515
00:29:19,760 --> 00:29:21,040
He's holding Emma's backpack.

516
00:29:21,160 --> 00:29:22,400
What's going on?

517
00:29:24,440 --> 00:29:25,800
Where is he going?

518
00:29:25,880 --> 00:29:27,280
Why is he after her?

519
00:29:30,600 --> 00:29:31,320
Thanks.

520
00:29:31,400 --> 00:29:33,040
On the 8th, Ken had a fight
with the girl.

521
00:29:33,160 --> 00:29:34,800
Do you know what happened?

522
00:29:34,880 --> 00:29:37,840
We never butt into other people's business.

523
00:29:37,920 --> 00:29:40,600
After they left, did the girl come back?

524
00:29:40,680 --> 00:29:42,320
No. Neither did.

525
00:29:43,520 --> 00:29:44,400
Thanks.

526
00:29:46,000 --> 00:29:48,000
Excuse me, is it time's up for me?

527
00:29:48,080 --> 00:29:49,440
Yes. It's time.

528
00:29:49,520 --> 00:29:50,600
Here's the key.

529
00:29:50,680 --> 00:29:51,360
Thanks.

530
00:29:51,760 --> 00:29:54,720
From the CCTV, they didn't look like
boyfriend and girlfriend.

531
00:29:54,840 --> 00:29:57,200
But Emma told me Ken was her boyfriend.

532
00:29:57,600 --> 00:30:00,880
Anyhow, Emma was bleeding when
she came out.

533
00:30:00,960 --> 00:30:02,320
It's definitely Ken's doing.

534
00:30:02,400 --> 00:30:04,360
Maybe he wanted to take all the money.

535
00:30:04,440 --> 00:30:06,960
That's why he went after your sister.

536
00:30:07,040 --> 00:30:09,440
Now that we have the CCTV footage,

537
00:30:09,520 --> 00:30:11,680
why don't we hand it to the Police?

538
00:30:11,800 --> 00:30:13,840
I don't think we should go to the Police.

539
00:30:13,920 --> 00:30:15,640
Once they start to investigate,

540
00:30:15,760 --> 00:30:17,320
they may find out you don't have an ID.

541
00:30:17,920 --> 00:30:20,360
The CCTV footage didn't show
Ken making any moves.

542
00:30:20,480 --> 00:30:22,160
It can only prove he had a motive.

543
00:30:23,560 --> 00:30:25,360
How about this?

544
00:30:25,440 --> 00:30:30,640
I'm leaving Hong Kong in a few days.

545
00:30:30,760 --> 00:30:32,840
By then, you can give the footage
to the Police.

546
00:30:33,240 --> 00:30:34,640
You're leaving?

547
00:30:34,840 --> 00:30:38,560
I'm leaving with Mom and Daddy
in a few days.

548
00:30:38,920 --> 00:30:40,880
When will you be back?

549
00:30:41,040 --> 00:30:42,560
Not for a while.

550
00:30:46,000 --> 00:30:47,920
I didn't really want to leave,

551
00:30:48,000 --> 00:30:51,360
but Daddy was afraid if we stayed,

552
00:30:51,440 --> 00:30:54,480
the Police will eventually find out
we have no IDs.

553
00:30:54,720 --> 00:30:58,040
That's why he decided to take Mom
back to her hometown.

554
00:30:58,120 --> 00:31:00,960
We'll never see each other again?

555
00:31:07,240 --> 00:31:08,760
Your name, Sir?

556
00:31:08,840 --> 00:31:09,920
Big Keung sent me.

557
00:31:10,040 --> 00:31:10,480
Let's go.

558
00:31:10,520 --> 00:31:11,360
Wait, buddy!

559
00:31:11,480 --> 00:31:14,160
How long will it take to get to
Meow Lung Kee?

560
00:31:14,280 --> 00:31:15,880
What?

561
00:31:16,200 --> 00:31:17,920
I heard of Meow Lung Kee.

562
00:31:18,040 --> 00:31:19,360
We'll go to Meow Lung Kee in a few days

563
00:31:19,480 --> 00:31:21,120
and we're all set.

564
00:31:21,360 --> 00:31:23,200
Can I run to the toilet across the street?

565
00:31:23,320 --> 00:31:24,240
Let me remind you,

566
00:31:24,360 --> 00:31:26,640
if you miss this ride, the next one
is in two weeks.

567
00:31:26,720 --> 00:31:28,520
I'll take a picture.
This may be related to Ken.

568
00:31:33,040 --> 00:31:34,360
(Kwan Sir)

569
00:31:34,800 --> 00:31:35,760
Kwan Sir?

570
00:31:35,920 --> 00:31:38,960
You told me before there's something
fishy about this Ken.

571
00:31:39,040 --> 00:31:41,200
We found out he's skipping town tonight.

572
00:31:41,320 --> 00:31:43,200
Have you heard anything?

573
00:31:43,360 --> 00:31:44,760
Ken is running away tonight?

574
00:31:44,840 --> 00:31:47,200
Let me go find out. Call you back.

575
00:31:47,280 --> 00:31:48,320
Bye!

576
00:31:48,480 --> 00:31:50,480
What? Ken is skipping town?

577
00:31:50,600 --> 00:31:53,280
Hurry up and tell him what we found out.

578
00:31:53,360 --> 00:31:55,080
No. You're still in Hong Kong.

579
00:31:55,200 --> 00:31:58,480
No, maybe nothing will happen.

580
00:31:58,560 --> 00:31:59,680
Why?

581
00:31:59,760 --> 00:32:01,560
When I went to HKIU to look for Ken,

582
00:32:01,640 --> 00:32:04,160
I told him I was Emma's sister.

583
00:32:04,240 --> 00:32:05,880
Emma's sister?

584
00:32:06,000 --> 00:32:09,120
He looked quite stunned. He didn't know.

585
00:32:09,200 --> 00:32:10,560
I don't understand.

586
00:32:10,640 --> 00:32:11,680
When Emma left,

587
00:32:11,800 --> 00:32:15,360
she promised she won't tell anyone
about our family.

588
00:32:15,440 --> 00:32:18,760
I suspect she never told Ken about us.

589
00:32:18,880 --> 00:32:20,480
Even if Ken was arrested,

590
00:32:20,560 --> 00:32:21,920
he won't have much to tell.

591
00:32:22,120 --> 00:32:23,800
I'll call Kwan Sir right now.

592
00:32:29,760 --> 00:32:32,080
Kwan Sir, I got something.

593
00:32:32,560 --> 00:32:33,640
Hello?

594
00:32:33,760 --> 00:32:35,680
Elsa, where are you?

595
00:32:35,840 --> 00:32:37,840
Me? I'm home.

596
00:32:38,000 --> 00:32:41,200
Really? Stay home and keep an eye on Mom.

597
00:32:41,360 --> 00:32:43,800
I'm busy at the hospital.
I'll be home later.

598
00:32:43,880 --> 00:32:45,520
OK! Bye!

599
00:32:45,640 --> 00:32:47,120
Meow Lung Kee.

600
00:32:47,200 --> 00:32:48,000
Copy.

601
00:32:48,080 --> 00:32:49,440
I'll get someone to follow up
on the license plate

602
00:32:49,600 --> 00:32:50,880
and see if we can intercept it.

603
00:32:51,040 --> 00:32:52,040
Keep in touch.

604
00:32:52,640 --> 00:32:53,520
Bye!

605
00:32:54,360 --> 00:32:57,840
OK, let's leave it to the Police.

606
00:32:57,920 --> 00:32:59,600
Hopefully, they'll catch Ken.

607
00:32:59,680 --> 00:33:02,880
Don't worry. Kwan Sir will call me
once he hears anything.

608
00:33:02,960 --> 00:33:06,080
If he's arrested, this whole thing is over.

609
00:33:07,080 --> 00:33:11,560
I'll take you home...somewhere nearby.

610
00:33:29,240 --> 00:33:33,160
I'm leaving with Mom and Daddy
in a few days.

611
00:33:34,240 --> 00:33:37,440
You're leaving?

612
00:33:45,120 --> 00:33:46,760
When will you be back?

613
00:33:48,720 --> 00:33:50,560
I really didn't want to leave.

614
00:33:54,120 --> 00:33:56,000
We have a few more days.

615
00:33:56,080 --> 00:33:58,000
Your supplies or any medication,

616
00:33:58,080 --> 00:33:59,760
you must bring them with you.

617
00:34:00,160 --> 00:34:03,360
They may be hard to find in a new place.

618
00:34:05,920 --> 00:34:08,280
When you pack, don't worry about weight.

619
00:34:08,400 --> 00:34:10,400
Bring everything you need.

620
00:34:10,600 --> 00:34:13,440
Make sure you have a jacket,
don't catch a cold.

621
00:34:16,400 --> 00:34:18,080
I'll wait for you to call.

622
00:34:34,480 --> 00:34:35,760
I'll get off here.

623
00:34:35,840 --> 00:34:37,280
Please stop the car.

624
00:35:02,720 --> 00:35:04,160
(Your transaction record has been sent
to your email)

625
00:35:04,240 --> 00:35:06,960
Someone checked Emma's Hong Kong Pass
transaction record on her email.

626
00:35:07,040 --> 00:35:08,480
Was it Elsa?

627
00:35:09,840 --> 00:35:11,600
Elsa, where are you?

628
00:35:11,720 --> 00:35:13,720
Me? I'm home.

629
00:35:13,800 --> 00:35:18,320
Really? Stay home and keep an eye on Mom.

630
00:35:18,520 --> 00:35:20,880
I'm busy at the hospital.
I'll be home later.

631
00:35:37,120 --> 00:35:38,160
Bye!

632
00:35:44,680 --> 00:35:46,640
Let's meet again before I leave.

633
00:35:47,240 --> 00:35:48,760
I'll wait for your message.

634
00:36:10,680 --> 00:36:11,280
Mom?

635
00:36:11,400 --> 00:36:12,800
Why did you come home late?

636
00:36:12,920 --> 00:36:13,920
What is it?

637
00:36:18,680 --> 00:36:21,600
Daddy? You said you'll be home later.

638
00:36:21,680 --> 00:36:23,520
You also said you were home.

639
00:36:23,840 --> 00:36:25,120
Where were you?

640
00:36:25,200 --> 00:36:26,400
When I was on my way home,

641
00:36:26,520 --> 00:36:28,560
I suddenly want to go to the library and...

642
00:36:28,680 --> 00:36:30,240
Stop lying!

643
00:36:30,680 --> 00:36:32,160
Who was that guy?

644
00:36:32,640 --> 00:36:35,280
Nobody. We met at the library.

645
00:36:35,360 --> 00:36:36,240
I met him once or twice.

646
00:36:36,360 --> 00:36:37,920
He dropped me off on his way.

647
00:36:38,040 --> 00:36:40,320
Don't worry, he doesn't know where I live.

648
00:36:40,440 --> 00:36:42,240
I got out at the market.

649
00:36:42,440 --> 00:36:44,200
So he's not just an ordinary friend.

650
00:36:44,520 --> 00:36:46,080
Don't see him again.

651
00:36:46,160 --> 00:36:47,440
I want you to stay home the next few days.

652
00:36:47,600 --> 00:36:48,640
Why?

653
00:36:48,760 --> 00:36:50,760
Felix, don't do this.

654
00:36:50,840 --> 00:36:52,400
I saw him at the library.

655
00:36:52,520 --> 00:36:53,920
He seems nice.

656
00:36:54,040 --> 00:36:56,400
He's very nice and he's good to me.

657
00:36:57,000 --> 00:36:58,960
So you're more than friends.

658
00:37:00,080 --> 00:37:01,920
Did you tell him about your family?

659
00:37:02,040 --> 00:37:04,800
You didn't tell him, right?

660
00:37:04,920 --> 00:37:06,320
Yes or no?

661
00:37:06,480 --> 00:37:09,280
I didn't mean to. But he was smart.

662
00:37:09,400 --> 00:37:10,720
I mentioned a thing or two

663
00:37:10,880 --> 00:37:12,400
and he figured out the rest.

664
00:37:12,520 --> 00:37:14,720
Smart guy? What does he do?

665
00:37:14,800 --> 00:37:17,760
He is...a reporter.

666
00:37:17,840 --> 00:37:20,240
He promised he won't tell anyone about us.

667
00:37:20,320 --> 00:37:22,400
You told a reporter about us?

668
00:37:22,520 --> 00:37:24,880
Daddy, I'm a grown up.

669
00:37:25,000 --> 00:37:27,120
I can tell a good guy from a baddie.

670
00:37:27,200 --> 00:37:29,200
YY is a good guy.

671
00:37:29,280 --> 00:37:31,760
He promised he won't tell anyone about us.

672
00:37:31,920 --> 00:37:33,720
Besides, once he found out about Emma,

673
00:37:33,800 --> 00:37:36,120
he tried very hard to find the killer.

674
00:37:36,200 --> 00:37:37,640
Why bother?

675
00:37:37,760 --> 00:37:40,720
I told you, leave that to the Police.

676
00:37:40,800 --> 00:37:42,760
But the Police didn't know about Emma.

677
00:37:42,920 --> 00:37:43,920
What can they do?

678
00:37:44,080 --> 00:37:46,000
I just want the catch the killer.

679
00:37:46,120 --> 00:37:48,080
So what if you did? Call the Police?

680
00:37:48,240 --> 00:37:49,760
And get you and Mom arrested?

681
00:37:49,920 --> 00:37:51,600
You won't rest until everyone is arrested?

682
00:37:51,760 --> 00:37:53,040
I'm so disappointed in you.

683
00:37:53,160 --> 00:37:55,120
I did everything for this family.

684
00:37:55,200 --> 00:37:56,400
But you did not.

685
00:37:56,520 --> 00:37:58,880
You told a reporter everything about us.

686
00:37:59,080 --> 00:38:02,320
Give me your phone. Go to your room.

687
00:38:02,400 --> 00:38:04,240
Get in...
I promised I won't stay.

688
00:38:04,360 --> 00:38:05,840
Get in.

689
00:38:06,840 --> 00:38:10,400
Let me out. I promised to go with you.

690
00:38:10,480 --> 00:38:12,000
Let me just see him for the last time.

691
00:38:12,200 --> 00:38:15,600
Mom...
Felix, calm down!

692
00:38:15,680 --> 00:38:17,600
You want Elsa to be like Emma?

693
00:38:26,880 --> 00:38:31,920
The key is for us to leave together.

694
00:38:32,080 --> 00:38:36,160
I won't let her and the reporter
ruin things for us.

695
00:38:40,400 --> 00:38:43,360
Kwan Sir, did you catch Ken?

696
00:38:43,440 --> 00:38:45,760
We busted him. We're taking his statement.

697
00:38:45,920 --> 00:38:47,920
Wait for me in the reception room
at the Station.

698
00:38:48,240 --> 00:38:50,320
Elsa, did you get home?

699
00:38:50,440 --> 00:38:52,400
Did anyone know you went out?

700
00:38:52,600 --> 00:38:55,120
Kwan Sir just told me they arrested Ken.

701
00:38:55,200 --> 00:38:57,240
Why didn't you text me?

702
00:38:57,360 --> 00:38:58,800
I'm worried about you.

703
00:38:59,400 --> 00:39:00,960
YY!
Kwan Sir?

704
00:39:01,960 --> 00:39:03,520
How did you find Ken?

705
00:39:03,680 --> 00:39:05,240
What and where is Meow Lung Kee?

706
00:39:05,320 --> 00:39:06,720
Meow Lung Kee is a code name

707
00:39:06,800 --> 00:39:07,720
for Ngan Kai Bay Pier in Sai Kung,

708
00:39:07,800 --> 00:39:09,600
where people on the run get on
and off speedboats.

709
00:39:09,680 --> 00:39:12,000
He's skipping town?
Because he killed someone?

710
00:39:12,120 --> 00:39:14,480
We checked the CCTV at the guesthouse.

711
00:39:14,600 --> 00:39:16,480
We confirmed the girl's name was Emma.

712
00:39:16,600 --> 00:39:19,360
Ken only admitted he wounded her
and tried to take her money.

713
00:39:19,480 --> 00:39:21,040
But he didn't kill her.

714
00:39:21,160 --> 00:39:22,960
She said she wanted to leave town.

715
00:39:23,040 --> 00:39:26,560
Since I have connections to
a human trafficking cartel,

716
00:39:26,640 --> 00:39:28,400
I put her in that guesthouse

717
00:39:28,520 --> 00:39:32,080
where people waiting to skip town
usually lie low for a while.

718
00:39:32,160 --> 00:39:33,520
Did you contact her afterwards?

719
00:39:33,640 --> 00:39:35,840
No. She's been looking for me

720
00:39:35,920 --> 00:39:37,120
asking me when the boat is ready.

721
00:39:37,200 --> 00:39:38,720
Look, I'm just the go-between,

722
00:39:38,800 --> 00:39:39,920
I don't know how it works.

723
00:39:40,000 --> 00:39:41,120
So I was dodging her

724
00:39:41,200 --> 00:39:42,480
because she was a pain.

725
00:39:42,680 --> 00:39:44,320
Lee, have you seen Ken?

726
00:39:44,440 --> 00:39:46,320
He was here just now.

727
00:39:46,440 --> 00:39:47,720
Don't know where he went.

728
00:39:48,280 --> 00:39:50,880
Why did you go to the guesthouse alone
on the 8th?

729
00:39:50,960 --> 00:39:53,720
I was in debt after I lost a lot of money
in the stock market.

730
00:39:53,880 --> 00:39:56,120
I saw the money she took from her family.

731
00:39:56,200 --> 00:39:59,840
I wanted to take it while she went out.

732
00:40:03,920 --> 00:40:05,040
What are you doing?

733
00:40:23,160 --> 00:40:27,040
Sir...she got all her money back.

734
00:40:27,120 --> 00:40:29,440
I really didn't kill her. Trust me.

735
00:40:29,640 --> 00:40:32,200
Ken said she was gone when
he went downstairs

736
00:40:32,280 --> 00:40:34,640
and he went to a bonesetter.

737
00:40:34,720 --> 00:40:36,000
My colleague checked out his story.

738
00:40:36,120 --> 00:40:37,360
He was telling the truth.

739
00:40:37,440 --> 00:40:39,120
So he had an alibi?

740
00:40:39,240 --> 00:40:40,400
Not exactly.

741
00:40:40,560 --> 00:40:43,600
Based on the CCTV and the medical
examiner's autopsy report,

742
00:40:43,680 --> 00:40:46,880
the estimated time of death should be
between night time on the 8th and the 10th.

743
00:40:47,000 --> 00:40:48,200
During this time frame,

744
00:40:48,280 --> 00:40:50,320
Ken was hiding in a friend's village house.

745
00:40:50,440 --> 00:40:52,640
But his friend was out of town.

746
00:40:52,720 --> 00:40:55,120
So he didn't actually have an alibi.

747
00:40:55,280 --> 00:40:57,640
Is it possible after he killed her,

748
00:40:57,720 --> 00:41:00,000
he made up a story about being
somewhere else?

749
00:41:00,080 --> 00:41:02,320
It's also possible he's not the killer.

750
00:41:02,400 --> 00:41:05,240
The place we found the body was deserted.

751
00:41:05,320 --> 00:41:06,560
There was only one store nearby.

752
00:41:06,720 --> 00:41:08,400
We didn't get much from the store owner.

753
00:41:08,600 --> 00:41:09,640
But there was a regular customer

754
00:41:09,720 --> 00:41:12,400
who claimed he saw something
suspicious on the night of the 8th.

755
00:41:12,520 --> 00:41:14,200
I didn't think much of it at first.

756
00:41:14,360 --> 00:41:16,480
But after I came back from my trip

757
00:41:16,560 --> 00:41:18,320
and saw the news of the faceless corpse,

758
00:41:18,440 --> 00:41:20,320
I began to sense something fishy.

759
00:41:20,400 --> 00:41:22,560
I remember after my hike on the 8th,

760
00:41:22,640 --> 00:41:24,240
I bought something to drink at the store.

761
00:41:24,320 --> 00:41:26,800
At a distance, I saw a man chasing a girl

762
00:41:26,920 --> 00:41:29,160
and followed her up the hill.

763
00:41:29,240 --> 00:41:31,520
Did you see his face?

764
00:41:31,640 --> 00:41:32,480
I didn't.

765
00:41:32,600 --> 00:41:34,720
He was quite far from me.

766
00:41:34,880 --> 00:41:37,440
Can you describe him?

767
00:41:37,600 --> 00:41:41,040
He's quite tall, at least 175 cm.

768
00:41:41,200 --> 00:41:45,440
He was wearing a dark green windbreaker.

769
00:41:45,560 --> 00:41:49,760
175 cm? How tall is Ken?

770
00:41:49,960 --> 00:41:51,760
He's not 175 cm tall.

771
00:41:51,960 --> 00:41:54,000
If the guy at the store was correct,

772
00:41:54,120 --> 00:41:57,920
the man who chased the girl was not Ken.

773
00:41:58,040 --> 00:41:59,840
Then who was it?

774
00:41:59,960 --> 00:42:04,000
Ken gave us a vital piece of information.

775
00:42:04,200 --> 00:42:06,520
He said he wasn't the victim's boyfriend.

776
00:42:06,600 --> 00:42:10,000
Her boyfriend is British, someone called
Chan Lap-jim.

777
00:42:13,800 --> 00:42:14,720
Look!

778
00:42:18,680 --> 00:42:24,400
C628, with the initials EH engraved
on the watchband.

779
00:42:24,520 --> 00:42:25,920
That's her watch!

780
00:42:26,040 --> 00:42:27,440
He's not only tall.

781
00:42:27,560 --> 00:42:30,000
He also has a dark green windbreaker.

782
00:42:30,720 --> 00:42:32,680
He's the killer?
